Task 2:
///Lab: Forced OAuth profile linking///

Open the site and log in with the simple credentials. After you loggen in you will se a "Attach a social profile" button. click on it and log in with the given credentials. Log out, and now you can log in with your
social profile. The site will log you in automatically. Check this login procedure in burp. Yo got 2 GET requests one with /auth?client_id.... and one with /oauth-linking?code=...
Notice that the first request sends the url with the authorization code for the second request. Maybe we can use this out.
Log out. go to my account and turn on intercept. Click on login with social profile forward the requests until you get the /oauth-linking request. Click on the request with right mouse button and copy the url out,
then drop the request. Go to exploit server, and create an iframe for this url:
<iframe src="https://0ab600ab04b408da806c03fc00380083.web-security-academy.net/oauth-linking?code=N9wjjmEMKpPAPGUgrTTFv8vEDdd14-5zhxw2nohqWid"></iframe>
Store it, deliver to the victim. Next time you log in with your social profile you will be admin, and you can delete carlos

Task 3:
///Lab: Stealing OAuth access tokens via an open redirect///

Open the site and log in. After you logged in check the requests and notice that there is a GET /me request where the website makes an API call, then using tihs request to fetch the user info:
{"sub":"wiener","apikey":"b4NVHTmVYrLqwprdBCDnPsOKVQieVrua","name":"Peter Wiener","email":"wiener@hotdog.com","email_verified":true}
Send this request to repeater. Log out and then click on my account and you will log in automatically. If you look at this process there is a GET /auth?client_id=tfst74oqx1vv7f4237sst&redirect_uri=...request which
is vulnerable to directory traversal. If you change the redirection url to https://0af000030304da9f808503d80078009d.web-security-academy.net/oauth-callback/../post?postId=1&response_type=token&nonce=-25633173&scope=openid%20profile%20email HTTP/2
it will redirect you to the first post after logged you in. Auditin the post page at the end of the page you will see a next post which is redirecting to you to the next post. click on it and send the request to repeater.
Modify the GET /post/next?path=/post?postId=2 to GET /post/next?path=abc.com and it will redirect you to abc.com. We will combine these vulnerabilites.
Create this malicios url:
